 ],
 "text": "She sent him 47 paper planes before she ever heard his voice. This is plane number one. Mira was 22, on the fifth floor of a city that never noticed her. Across the alley, a stranger kept his lamp on until 2 a.m. every single night. One night, she folded her grocery list into a plane and threw it. It landed right on his windowsill. His lamp went off. Great, she'd scared him. But the next morning, it flew back. On the back of her list, he'd drawn her. Badly. And underneath, a tiny lamp and a question mark. So that night, she folded plane number two. Just one word. Hi. But the wind had other plans. It dropped five floors into the alley, where someone picked it up. And it wasn't him."
